CSE 363 HW4 - Infostealer Implant
SBUID: 115201424

DESCRIPTION
tmp363.py   
Malware implant. Scans /home/ for sensitive files, archives and
encrypts them in memory, exfiltrates to server over TCP.
server363.py 
Receiving server. Decrypts and extracts received data into a
timestamped subdirectory per victim.

DEPENDENCIES
sudo apt install python3-cryptography

DESIGN CHOICES
- AES-256 CBC with PKCS7 padding for encryption
- In-memory ZIP using BytesIO (no disk writes on implant)
- Plain TCP with 4-byte length header
- Targets: ~/.ssh/, ~/.config/, ~/.aws/, ~/.gcloud/, ~/.azure/, ~/.*_history

USAGE
- python3 server363.py 127.0.0.1 1234
- sudo python3 tmp363.py 127.0.0.1 1234
